---
import Layout from "@layouts/ComponentsLayout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Cookie banner</h1>
  <p class="govuk-body-l">
    Allow users to accept or reject cookies which are not essential to making
    your service work.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Example</h2>
  <div
    class="govuk-cookie-banner"
    data-nosnippet
    role="region"
    aria-label="Cookie banner"
  >
    <div class="govuk-cookie-banner__message govuk-width-container">
      <div class="govuk-grid-row">
        <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
          <h2 class="govuk-cookie-banner__heading govuk-heading-m">
            Cookies on this government service
          </h2>
          <div class="govuk-cookie-banner__content">
            <p class="govuk-body">
              We use analytics cookies to help understand how users use our
              service.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-button-group">
        <button
          type="submit"
          value="accept"
          name="cookies"
          class="govuk-button"
          data-module="govuk-button"
        >
          Accept analytics cookies
        </button>
        <button
          type="submit"
          value="reject"
          name="cookies"
          class="govuk-button"
          data-module="govuk-button"
        >
          Reject analytics cookies
        </button>
        <a class="govuk-link" href="/cookie-preferences"
          >View cookie preferences</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:START (auto-generated - edited content will be overwritten by scripts/update-component-guidance.mjs) -->
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">When to use this component</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use this component if your service sets any cookies on a user’s device.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">Remember, you must:</p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>tell users about the cookies your service sets on their device</li>
    <li>
      let users accept or reject any cookies that are not essential to providing
      your service
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="govuk-body">The term ‘non-essential cookies’ includes:</p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>HTML5 local storage</li>
    <li>service workers</li>
    <li>any other technologies that store files on the user’s device</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    This cookie banner and the <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://design-system.service.gov.uk/patterns/cookies-page/"
      >Cookies page pattern</a
    > are based on the approach to getting cookie consent used on the GOV.UK website.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    This component page shows several options for using a cookie banner, based
    on the types of cookies you’re using in the service. We also tell you what
    to cover in your cookie banner, with some text examples.
  </p>
  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">Before you start</h3>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://design-system.service.gov.uk/patterns/cookies-page/#auditing-and-categorising-your-cookies"
      >Audit and categorise your cookies</a
    > as shown in the cookies page pattern to help you choose the best option for
    your service.
  </p>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    You must not take the information on this page as legal advice. Your
    organisation is responsible and accountable for what they do to comply with
    data protection legislation, such as:
  </p>
  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR)</li>
    <li>General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Check with your organisation's privacy expert to see how data protection
    legislation affects your website and service.
  </p>
  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:END -->
</Layout>
